=== INVESTIGATION ===

Web page (web/src/features/vehicles/pages/VehicleListPage.tsx, 462 lines) is the "Fleet"
list. Data sources (manifest): `fetchVehicleState(id) → GET /vehicles/{id}/state` (batched
per vehicle for the summary + battery panel) and `usePinned('vehicle') → GET
/pinned?type=vehicle` (pin order). The page itself also issues the implicit
`useQuery(['vehicles']) → GET /vehicles` list query and the `syncMut`
(POST /vehicles/sync) + `deleteMut` (DELETE /vehicles/{id}) + `useTogglePin` mutations.
SI display contract: `rated_range` / `odometer` are SI metres, `charger_power` is SI watts
(cf. the sibling feature-view VehicleCardLiveState), `speed` is SI m/s; the page converts at
the render boundary via `convertDistanceFromSI` / `formatDistance` (`useUnits`) and renders
`fmtNumber` at the user precision (web `_globalPrecision`, default 2).

Parity manifest record (37 = 9 panels + 4 states + 24 strings):
  panels  : GlassPanel1 (load-error), GlassPanel2 (sync-success banner),
            GlassPanel3 (sync-error banner), Total-Vehicles, Avg-Battery,
            MetricCard6 (Total-Range), Charging-Online (4× MetricCard),
            GlassPanel8 (Fleet Battery Status), GlassPanel9 (per-vehicle card)
  charts  : 0     maps : 0
  states  : loading, empty, error, success
  strings : 24 web keys (common.delete, common.noData, nav.vehicles, 21× vehicles.*)

Region map (web → native):
  • error branch `<GlassPanel><p text-red-500>{loadError}</p>`        → VehicleListErrorPanel (GlassPanel1)
  • syncMut.isSuccess `<GlassPanel green>{syncSuccess}`               → VehicleListSyncBanner .success (GlassPanel2)
  • syncMut.isError `<GlassPanel red>{syncError}`                     → VehicleListSyncBanner .failure (GlassPanel3)
  • 4× `<MetricCard label value icon color>`                         → VehicleFleetSummaryGrid (shared MetricCard, P3)
  • `<GlassPanel>` "Fleet Battery Status" + per-vehicle bars         → FleetBatteryPanel (GlassPanel8; common.noData empty)
  • `<StaggerContainer><GlassPanel hover>` per vehicle               → VehicleListCardList + VehicleListRow (GlassPanel9)
  • `vehicleList.length === 0 ? <EmptyState>`                        → VehicleListEmptyView (empty state)
  • `isLoading ? <VehicleListSkeleton>`                              → VehicleListSkeleton (loading state)
  • `toast.success/error` + `<ConfirmDialog>`                        → VehicleListToastView + .confirmationDialog
  • web DataFreshnessAuto header chip is NOT a manifest parity item and the vehicles list is
    a poll (no SSE) — no >2-min staleness indicator is required for this unit (ADR-013 N/A).

PREDECESSOR / COLLISION FINDING (binding for the whole implementation):
  A sibling Vehicles port already exists at apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Vehicles/
  VehicleDetail* (PUBLIC VehicleDetailPage/Model/…); the feature-view bundle owns the PUBLIC
  axes `VehicleStatus` (web deriveVehicleStatus + FSM tokens) and `BatteryTone` (web
  batteryColor thresholds) in VehicleCard.Adapter.swift. Both compile into the SINGLE
  TeslaSync module (project.yml), and Swift forbids (a) two same-name types and (b) two
  same-basename files in one target. Pre-grep confirmed ZERO existing VehicleList* symbols
  and ZERO VehicleList* file basenames. Resolution: every type + file in this unit is
  `VehicleList…`-prefixed, and the shared `VehicleStatus` / `BatteryTone` axes + the P2
  tokens + P3 components (MetricCard, GlassPanel, EmptyState, Skeleton, FadeIn/Stagger,
  Button, typography) + P1 Units facade are REUSED (DRY), not duplicated. The unit lives in
  the prescribed directory apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Vehicles/.

STRING-CATALOG FINDING:
  Localizable.xcstrings already carried `common.delete` ("Delete") and `common.noData`
  ("No data available"). The remaining 22 bare keys (nav.vehicles + 21 vehicles.*) were added
  with the verbatim web English defaults taken from web/src/i18n/en.json + the source
  `t(key, default)` fallbacks. `vehicles.emptyMessage` has no en.json entry — added from the
  inline source default. `vehicles.removeMessage` uses `%@` (resolved via String(format:)) for
  the web i18next `{{name}}` interpolation. Five small a11y-label keys (pin.pin, pin.unpin,
  vehicles.open, vehicles.locked, vehicles.sentry) were added for VoiceOver (additive; NOT
  parity-tracked). JSON re-validated (12145 → 12172 keys).

DECISION — charger_power units:
  The web row renders `{state.charger_power} kW` verbatim. The repo's own VehicleCardLiveState
  documents `charger_power` as SI WATTS, so the model stores `chargerPowerW` (SI) and the chip
  formats through `Units.formatPower` at the display boundary — yielding the same "{n} kW"
  while honoring the no-non-SI-on-disk rule (ADR-005 / SI cutover).

DECISION — status chip text:
  The web badge renders the RAW lowercase status word (`<Badge>{status}</Badge>`, not a
  translated label), so VehicleStatusChip shows `status.rawValue` verbatim (no invented i18n
  key) tinted by the shared `VehicleStatus.tone`.

DECISION — pin affordance:
  The manifest's tracked `usePinned` source is bound in the model for BOTH the pinned-first
  sort (web `sortedVehicleList`) and each row's pinned state; the row's pin button is a
  lightweight toggle calling `model.togglePin` (one source of truth) rather than threading the
  standalone shared PinButton's bucket-scoped PinnedStore through the page model.

DECISION — data states:
  The web derives empty inside the loaded body (`vehicleList.length === 0`); the model promotes
  it to a distinct `.empty` case so all four manifest data states (loading/empty/error/success)
  are first-class and individually evidenced. GlassPanel8 additionally carries the
  fetchVehicleState empty (`common.noData`) when no per-vehicle state resolved.

