Design notes:
  - @Observable `VehicleListPageModel` consumes a KMP-bindable data-source seam (loadVehicles
    ← useQuery(['vehicles']); fetchVehicleState ← GET /vehicles/{id}/state; usePinned ←
    usePinned('vehicle'); syncVehicles/deleteVehicle/togglePin ← the mutations) — the view holds
    no networking (ADR-004). Derives avgBattery/totalRangeM/chargingCount/onlineCount (web `fleet`
    memo) over the resolved entries + the pinned-first stable sort (web `sortedVehicleList`).
    Per-vehicle states are fetched concurrently via a TaskGroup (web `Promise.all`), each failure
    → no state (web per-entry try/catch → null).
  - SI only on the model; conversion at the SwiftUI render boundary via `Units` (P1/S5) +
    `@Environment(\.tsUnits)` (ADR-005): distance metres→user unit (formatDistance / convertDistance
    + fmtNumber), power watts→kW (formatPower); battery percent + counts are unitless.
  - Adaptive macOS + iOS: ScrollView, 1100pt max content width, LazyVGrid stat cards reflow
    1→2→4 cols (.adaptive(minimum:220)); the vehicle card stacks its battery row over its metrics
    row; `.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.large)` iOS-gated; one adaptive SwiftUI source (ADR-002/006).
  - a11y: stat cards + battery panel rows + vehicle cards carry combined labels/traits; the card
    list is a labelled container; the name button is a link; pin/open/delete carry VoiceOver labels;
    dynamic Color.TS (light/dark/high-contrast), Dynamic Type via Font.TS, ≥44pt action targets
    (32pt glyph in a row tap area). Battery bars are decorative (accessibilityHidden) with the row
    carrying the reading (ADR-015).
  - No #Preview blocks authored (this SDK's #Preview macro is ambiguous between SwiftUI and
    AppKit/UIKit — the documented baseline breakage; see ENVIRONMENTAL NOTE) — keeps the unit
    clean-compiling. The Empty/Failing data-source seams remain for the P9 XCTest phase.

